      "description": "Hale Brothers built a ten-storey steel and reinforced concrete warehouse at the corner of Stevenson Street, L-shaped through to Mint Street, stuccoed with modest Classical Revival ornament and a rusticated second and third floor that echo the store across the alley. Its ground floor was used for more retail.",
